yo, for big json in python i usually just reach for ijson when the file won't fit in memory. streams it so you're not loading the whole thing at once. for normal sized stuff plain json.load is fine tbh.

only thing i'd add: if you're doing this a lot, write a tiny example script first with a sample file and a couple of test cases. saves you from guessing later.

@rapid_marten81 jq is a beast, agree. but once i'm in python land i kinda prefer staying there.

